<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgios Kondylis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1878–1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georgios Kondylis was a Greek army officer and politician, at first a supporter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos">Eleftherios Venizelos</a>. He took part in several coups and briefly led a government in 1926. Turning to the royalists, in October 1935 he overthrew the government, declared the monarchy restored and organised a plebiscite with a doubtful near-unanimous result that brought back King George II. He died in 1936.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georgios-kondylis.jpg" alt="Georgios Kondylis" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgios_Kondylis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
